.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt CMS_FINAL 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm CMS_final ,
.Nm CMS_final_digest
.Nd finalise a CMS_ContentInfo structure
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/cms.h
.Ft int
.Fo CMS_final
.Fa "CMS_ContentInfo *cms"
.Fa "BIO *data"
.Fa "BIO *dcont"
.Fa "unsigned int flags"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo CMS_final_digest
.Fa "CMS_ContentInfo *cms"
.Fa "const unsigned char *md"
.Fa "unsigned int mdlen"
.Fa "BIO *dcont"
.Fa "unsigned int flags"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn CMS_final
finalises the structure
.Fa cms .
Its purpose is to perform any operations necessary on
.Fa cms
(digest computation for example) and set the appropriate fields.
The parameter
.Fa data
contains the content to be processed.
The
.Fa dcont
parameter contains a BIO to write content to after processing: this is
only used with detached data and will usually be set to NULL.
.Pp
.Fn CMS_final_digest
finalises the structure
.Fa cms
using a pre-computed digest, rather than computing the digest from the
original data.
.Sh NOTES
These functions will normally be called when the
.Sy CMS_PARTIAL
flag is used.
It should only be used when streaming is not performed because the
streaming I/O functions perform finalisation operations internally.
.Pp
To sign a pre-computed digest,
.Xr CMS_sign 3
or
.Xr CMS_sign_ex 3
is called with the
.Fa data
parameter set to NULL before the CMS structure is finalised with the
digest provided to
.Fn CMS_final_digest
in binary form.
When signing a pre-computed digest, the security relies on the digest
and its computation from the original message being trusted.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn CMS_final
and
.Fn CMS_final_digest
return 1 for success or 0 for failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 ,
.Xr CMS_sign 3 ,
.Xr CMS_encrypt 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn CMS_final_digest
was added in OpenSSL 3.2.
